it('\\n'):\n    if re.search(r'experiment-repo|P6|P7|confirm|interval',l): print(l[:400])\n\" | head -40"]], "output": "```console\n47377\n# Outline — what the paper says and what carries it (revision 13: results of `experiment-repo`#6 applied; verdicts per claim; review #5 applied; Brief rev. 12: P6 κ* net of null cells, control C3, threshold floor; P7 analytic noise part)\nAdditions to the cell list (A = review item): **(A1)** fine s grid {0,0.1,…,0.9} × 6 mechanisms at core d, p=½ (~60 cells), and σ∈{0.25,0.5,1} on that row for the 2–3 mechanisms where the sign flips; **(A2)** n slice {1000, 3000, 10000} on (a),(c) at core d, p; **(A3)** cluster-design cells on graphs of different cluster quality (ER, SBM at weaker mixing, ego-Facebook and Stanford3 with detected c\n**Settled by `analysis` (plan rev. 1, `experiment-repo`#4):** A1 fine s grid at d∈{5,20,80}, p=½, with the caveat that (e) at s=0.9 is truncated at K=30 steps and `or_fit` stops at ρ=0.85, which Fig 1 states; A2/A3 as cluster cells on weak-mixing SBM, ego-Facebook, Stanford3 (γ∈{0.3,1,3}) with cluster count, modularity, conductance and the undefined-rate reported per run; the n slice (n∈{1000,3000\n**C2 — Bias is set by curvature × corner distance; independent of d for smooth responses in the fraction feature (with the mechanism qualifier below).** For a response curved in exposure, linear-fit spillover bias ≈ −½g''(1−2p) (+ third-order term); zero at p=½ to second order; for threshold responses with threshold outside the observed support the linear fit sees no spillover and the bias is the \n*What the paper says (rev. 7):* (a) verdict *not supported* by the rule (pooled point gain 0.034 < 0.05), worded as **no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score, not evidence of none**: the intervals [−0.28, 0.34] (leave-one-mechanism-out) and [−0.27, 0.22] (leave-one-family-out) contain both a useful and a useless score, on 6 mechanism groups and 7 families; this goes in the abstract and \n**C7 — Robustness to a wrong graph and to real graphs.** (Real graphs also appear in the headline map, Fig 1.) Edge-noise slice (mechanisms (a), (e) at core, d=20, p=½): every estimator builds features on a graph with 10%/30% of edges dropped/rewired; the oracle form stops being oracle; does S flag the added bias. Real graphs (socfb-Stanford3, ego-Facebook) with synthetic outcomes at the core sett\n**C8 — Inference: does the nominal 95% CI cover? (review A6)** Coverage and width of the unit bootstrap (Bernoulli), the cluster bootstrap (cluster designs), graph-aware variance where available and the oracle-spec interval, across cells. The practitioner's question, and the bootstrap SE is already a P5 benchmark. Prediction to test, not assume: coverage degrades where leverage is large (variance \n**C9 — An assumption-indexed extrapolation-sensitivity interval (Brief P6, rev. 11; exploratory-after-results on the existing cells, confirmatory on the shared block).** *Order of events, which the paper tells as it happened:* P5(ii) was predicted to work and failed; the non-identification argument was formulated afterwards as an explanation of the failure; P6 and P7 are the tests of that explanat\n## 3b. Where the results stand (rev. 6; verdicts are `analysis`'s, from `experiment-repo`#4 and `results/claims/` in `paper-repo`)\n| C1 variance ~ leverage | supported | log-log slopes at σ=0.5: n −0.504 [−0.514, −0.495], p(1−p) −0.504, **(1+d) +0.551 [0.547, 0.556]** | d exponent is 0.55, interval excludes ½: stated as 0.55 (exact leverage form), never as \"½\", and **the realised leverage scales as L ∝ n^−0.02 (1+d)^1.09 [p(1−p)]^−0.99 over 210 graph draws (`c1_L_exponents.csv`; run-level CI for the d exponent [1.08, 1.11]), \n| C2 bias = curvature × corner distance | supported where the account applies, **with d-dependence differing by mechanism** | exact population-OLS prediction (with the K=30 truncated operator the simulation uses and finite-n centring, `pred_bias_finite_n`) lies inside the MC interval in 86.6% of 1257 cells of (a)–(f) (85.1% without centring); (e) was 58% with the untruncated series, **81.4% with t\n| C4 \n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "bc6e92dc-5413-5c3b-865d-617e040427e0", "at": 1795652763.2492602, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 102639, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "103ac188413712dd326b089984befea9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "b8a2070f-dab2-5ae1-a22c-e4bf50af7de4", "at": 1795652763.259426, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 102641, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "103ac188413712dd326b089984befea9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "9c2f6d48-21e3-5332-ba9a-b6d89b043606", "at": 1795652763.2696338, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 102642, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "103ac188413712dd326b089984befea9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "19b4a9ca-a103-550f-bf18-71fe3f403f36", "at": 1795652763.4831831, "until": 1795652763.5321372, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 102645, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "collaboration.request", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "103ac188413712dd326b089984befea9", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "200", "label": "collaborate → 200", "repository": "world/story-repo", "